  "body_mappings": [
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        498.6614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        597.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "On 29 May 1919, as a total eclipse obscured the sun, two British expeditions photographed stars in its apparent vicinity. Arthur Eddington observed from Príncipe, an island off West Africa; Crommelin and Davidson from Sobral, in north-eastern Brazil. They were testing general relativity's bold prediction that the sun's gravity would deflect starlight."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        391.1614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        490.1614173228347
      ],
      "text": "On 6 November, at a joint meeting of the Royal Society and the Royal Astronomical Society, the findings were hailed as confirming it. The Times proclaimed a \"Revolution in Science\"; a New York Times headline read \"Lights All Askew in the Heavens\". Almost overnight, Einstein, eminent among physicists, became a global celebrity."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        283.6614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        382.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "Stockholm proved harder to dazzle. The Nobel physics committee valued rigorous experimental confirmation, and committee member Allvar Gullstrand, a Nobel-winning eye specialist, deemed the empirical support for relativity insufficient. Since no nomination fulfilled Nobel's criteria, the 1921 prize was reserved for a year, as the statutes permit."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        156.3614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        275.1614173228347
      ],
      "text": "On 9 November 1922 the Royal Swedish Academy of Sciences conferred it on Einstein, citing his services to theoretical physics, especially his discovery of the law of the photoelectric effect. That law, which governs how light ejects electrons from metal, helped underpin quantum theory. A letter the next day clarified that the prize took no account of relativity. Einstein, then aboard a steamer bound for Japan, would miss the December ceremony."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        68.66141732283471,
        461.8976377952756,
        147.8614173228347
      ],
      "text": "On 11 July 1923, in Gothenburg, Sweden, he delivered his Nobel lecture before a congress of Nordic scientists, devoting it to the fundamental ideas and problems of relativity. The theory the committee looked past reached a Nobel podium after all, carried there by the man the prize had honoured."
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        517.6614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        597.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "1919年5月29日，一次全日食遮蔽了太阳，两支英国考察队拍摄了天空中看似位于太阳附近的恒星。阿瑟·爱丁顿观测于普林西比岛，这是一座岛，位于西非外海；克罗姆林和戴维森则在索布拉尔，位于巴西东北部。他们要检验广义相对论的一个大胆的预言，也就是太阳的引力会使经过它附近的星光偏折。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        429.1614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        509.1614173228347
      ],
      "text": "11月6日，英国皇家学会与皇家天文学会召开联席会议，观测结果被盛赞为证实了这一预言。《泰晤士报》宣告了一场“科学革命”；《纽约时报》的标题写着“天上的光全歪了”。几乎一夜之间，在物理学家中卓越的爱因斯坦成了举世皆知的名人。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        340.6614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        420.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "斯德哥尔摩却没那么容易被眩惑。诺贝尔物理学委员会看重的是严格的实验证实，而委员会成员阿尔瓦·古尔斯特兰德，一位获得过诺贝尔奖的眼科专家，认定相对论的实证支持不足。由于没有一项提名符合诺贝尔定下的标准，1921年的奖被保留一年，这是章程所允许的。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        252.16141732283472,
        461.8976377952756,
        332.1614173228347
      ],
      "text": "1922年11月9日，瑞典皇家科学院把这个奖授予爱因斯坦，表彰他对理论物理学的贡献，尤其是他发现了光电效应定律。这条定律决定了光如何把电子从金属中打出，曾帮助奠定量子理论的基础。第二天的一封信澄清，此奖并未考虑相对论。爱因斯坦当时正乘一艘开往日本的轮船，将错过12月的颁奖典礼。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        183.66141732283472,
        461.8976377952756,
        243.66141732283472
      ],
      "text": "1923年7月11日，在瑞典哥德堡，他发表了他的诺贝尔演讲，面向北欧自然科学家大会，专门讲相对论的基本思想与问题。委员会绕开不看的那个理论，终究登上了诺贝尔的讲台，把它带上去的，正是这个奖所嘉奖的爱因斯坦。"
    }
  ],
